From d97e262af3372b5053374d2c6962740a9448dab0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Johnny Collado <54557697+JohnnyC96@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 08:40:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/9] IOP: load buffer modules from IOP RAM; LOADFILE calls
 write the start result

sceSifLoadModuleBuffer and sceSifLoadStartModuleBuffer take a module that is already
in IOP memory: the game DMAs it there first (Biohazard Outbreak copies DRIVE.DAT to
IOP 0x120000 and passes IOP addresses). loadModuleBuffer read the image from EE RAM,
so these loads always failed. Read IOP RAM first, falling back to EE RAM for callers
that pass an EE address.

Also:
- buffer-loaded modules are recorded like path loads (observePhysicalLoad +
  rebuildRoutes) and named after their .iopmod name;
- _sceSifLoadModule and _sceSifLoadModuleBuffer, the libkernel functions behind the
  sceSifLoad(Start)Module(Buffer) wrappers, write the module's start result to *$a3
  (the game tests it: 1 means the module ended at once, e.g. no HDD);
- sceSifSearchModuleByName looks loaded modules up by .iopmod name (HLE modules by
  their key), via IopSubsystem::findModuleByName.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
